{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01365",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.14,
      "end_seconds": 6.44,
      "duration_seconds": 5.3,
      "text": "Doctor, hi, where would you like me to put my coat?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.53,
      "end_seconds": 12.05,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "Not at all, please sit. What seems to be wrong?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 13.58,
      "end_seconds": 22.07,
      "duration_seconds": 8.49,
      "text": "sorry, what was I saying, hello, doctor, I came in with them, if that's okay"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.57,
      "end_seconds": 30.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "Please do. Extra information is always welcome."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.73,
      "end_seconds": 39.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "I'm here because of watery diarrhoea."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 45.59,
      "end_seconds": 49.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "How long has it been like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 50.11,
      "end_seconds": 52.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "I'd say two weeks maybe"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 54.16,
      "end_seconds": 58.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "I think it's been nearer three weeks actually"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.91,
      "end_seconds": 63.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.34,
      "text": "okay, so roughly two to three weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.95,
      "end_seconds": 65.89,
      "duration_seconds": 0.94,
      "text": "Yeah roughly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 66.6,
      "end_seconds": 74.57,
      "duration_seconds": 7.97,
      "text": "can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.14,
      "end_seconds": 80.62,
      "duration_seconds": 5.48,
      "text": "it settles a little with oral rehydration it feels severe to me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.22,
      "end_seconds": 88.59,
      "duration_seconds": 7.37,
      "text": "And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 88.69,
      "end_seconds": 93.93,
      "duration_seconds": 5.24,
      "text": "Tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.57,
      "end_seconds": 122.27,
      "duration_seconds": 26.7,
      "text": "I was getting to that! Oh, and a low fever. Had that since yesterday. Ah, as for low fever, it happens all the time. Sorry, uh, what was I saying, I've also been feeling sick, since yesterday. As for feeling sick, I'd say every other day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.15,
      "end_seconds": 128.7,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "Have you noticed severe dehydration or blood in the stool?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 129.45,
      "end_seconds": 141.94,
      "duration_seconds": 12.49,
      "text": "No, no severe dehydration, no blood in the stool. I did have crampy tummy pain at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.74,
      "end_seconds": 146.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "and and vomiting, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.29,
      "end_seconds": 151.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "Not at all, no vomiting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 153.2,
      "end_seconds": 158.08,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice vomiting. He doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 158.68,
      "end_seconds": 164.44,
      "duration_seconds": 5.76,
      "text": "no I don't think I did maybe a little I'm not sure"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.98,
      "end_seconds": 172.29,
      "duration_seconds": 7.31,
      "text": "alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed any breathing difficulties apart from this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 173.53,
      "end_seconds": 175.31,
      "duration_seconds": 1.78,
      "text": "No, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.23,
      "end_seconds": 180.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "What do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 182.09,
      "end_seconds": 188.94,
      "duration_seconds": 6.85,
      "text": "It's a... um I can't remember what it's called. It's a round yellow one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.48,
      "end_seconds": 192.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "right do you remember what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.91,
      "end_seconds": 206.35,
      "duration_seconds": 12.44,
      "text": "For my migraines I believe. My son sets them out for me I just take what I'm given. Foracort inhaler twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.82,
      "end_seconds": 214.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "are there any illnesses in your family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 215.11,
      "end_seconds": 217.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "my cousin has psoriasis"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.48,
      "end_seconds": 237.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.84,
      "text": "has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 239.14,
      "end_seconds": 242.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "Well, not to my knowledge, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.82,
      "end_seconds": 255.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 257.17,
      "end_seconds": 266.28,
      "duration_seconds": 9.11,
      "text": "Eczema, for five years. I have migraines, for five years. Oh, I've had asthma for about a year now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.42,
      "end_seconds": 275.04,
      "duration_seconds": 7.62,
      "text": "alright, eczema and asthma, that matches what I have here what line of work are you in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 275.96,
      "end_seconds": 281.54,
      "duration_seconds": 5.58,
      "text": "I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.64,
      "end_seconds": 287.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "time for your numbers, if that's okay"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 300.0,
      "end_seconds": 301.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "sit still for a moment.."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 318.56,
      "end_seconds": 325.65,
      "duration_seconds": 7.09,
      "text": "Okay: heart rate 95, BP is 106 over 74. And temperature 38.5, saturation 95 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 326.87,
      "end_seconds": 329.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "Okay, time for me to examine you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 330.93,
      "end_seconds": 333.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "I'll listen to your chest now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 349.24,
      "end_seconds": 355.31,
      "duration_seconds": 6.07,
      "text": "your tummy is soft with mild general tenderness and your mouth is a little dry"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 359.71,
      "end_seconds": 369.47,
      "duration_seconds": 9.76,
      "text": "that's the examination finished. Okay, thinking it through, my working impression is travellers' diarrhoea. I can't rule out a parasitic infection yet"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 370.98,
      "end_seconds": 372.95,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "Is it dangerous, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 375.01,
      "end_seconds": 408.99,
      "duration_seconds": 33.98,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's travellers' diarrhoea and we'll know more once the a stool sample is back. I'll request a stool sample it'll help with diarrhoea after travel. Drink plenty of fluids and wash your hands carefully. One warning sign to remember: the symptoms get worse. In that case don't wait. I'd like you back if it lasts more than a week. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 410.03,
      "end_seconds": 413.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "great, thank you for your help"
    }
  ]
}